CONTEXT FROM TEXTBOOK:
This figure is a shaded three-dimensional cutaway drawing of a domed room built as a half-ellipsoid on a circular base. The outer shell carries a blue-to-white gradient and is cut away at the front so the viewer looks into the interior, where the inner surface and the floor are shaded warm tan; a thick gray band forms the base slab beneath the floor. Two small dark points on the floor mark the foci, labeled F' on the left and F on the right. A fan of dark blue segments with arrowheads leaves F', rises at a range of angles to strike the inside of the curved dome at several separated points, and reflects back down, every one arriving at F. The paths cross one another mid-room, and no two share a bounce point. Drawing many distinct routes between the same pair of labeled points emphasizes that the convergence holds no matter which direction a ray sets out in. The illustration accounts for the acoustics of a whispering chamber, where a person speaking softly at one focus of an elliptical dome is heard clearly by a listener at the other.

PROJECTION TYPE: perspective
Use the scaffold's true perspective projection after building all geometry. Use this only when the source has real vanishing-point convergence or distance-based size shrinkage; then depth should visibly affect apparent size.

ELEMENTS TO RECREATE IN 3D:
  - Half-ellipsoid dome shell, cut away across the front so the interior is visible
  - Outer surface of the dome with blue-to-white vertical gradient (deep blue at the rim, pale blue/white near the top)
  - Thin white/light highlight band along the cut rim showing the shell thickness
  - Inner surface of the dome shaded warm tan, visible through the cutaway
  - Horizontal shading band (tonal break) circling the inside of the dome about one-third up
  - Elliptical/circular floor disk of the room, warm tan with a light-to-dark gradient
  - Thick gray cylindrical base slab beneath the floor
  - Focus point F' — small dark blue dot on the left of the floor, on the major axis
  - Focus point F — small dark blue dot on the right of the floor, on the major axis
  - Text label "F'" below-left of the left focus, "F" below-right of the right focus
  - Seven dark navy outbound ray segments leaving F' at different upward angles
  - Seven dark navy return ray segments from each dome bounce point down to F
  - Arrowheads at the midpoint of each segment indicating direction of travel (up-and-away from F', down-and-toward F)
  - Distinct reflection (bounce) points spread across the inner dome surface, no two rays sharing one
  - Crossing pattern of rays in the middle of the room

GEOMETRY NOTES (world-space scale, color palette, and any formula/value needed for correctness — build to these so sizes, zoom, and colors match the source; do not guess dimensions the notes already specify):
Axes: +X screen-right (major axis of the room), +Y up, +Z toward viewer (depth). Dome = upper half of an ellipsoid with semi-axes a=3.0 in X, c=3.0 in Z, b=2.0 in Y, centered at origin; floor is the disk y=0, x²/9+z²/9≤1. Shell drawn with ~0.08 thickness; the front half (z>0 region in front of the cut plane z≈+1.1) is removed so the interior is visible. Gray base slab: cylinder radius 3.15, height 0.45, centered at y=−0.22, color #57585a with a lighter top lip #8d8e90. Floor tan gradient #f2e2bf (near) to #dcc79b (far). Dome outer gradient: deep blue #1f6ab0 at the rim rising to pale blue #b9dcf2 then near-white #f4fbff at the crown; cut-rim highlight strip #ffffff/#e8f2fa. Dome inner surface tan #e3cfa4 with a darker tonal band #cdb888 running horizontally around the interior at about y=0.7. Foci lie in the vertical XY cross-section (z=0) of the ellipse x²/9+y²/4=1: focal distance sqrt(9−4)=2.236, so F' at (−2.236, 0.02, 0) and F at (+2.236, 0.02, 0), drawn as dark navy dots radius ~0.09. Labels 'F'' and 'F' in italic serif, ~0.35 units below/outside each dot. Rays: all seven lie in the z=0 vertical plane and are dark navy #1c4e80, line width ~3px, with a single solid arrowhead at the midpoint of each segment. Each ray leaves F' at an upward angle, hits the ellipse boundary at a point P, and returns to F; total path |F'P|+|PF| = 2a = 6 for every ray (the defining ellipse property). Use seven well-separated bounce points on the ellipse, roughly at parameter angles t = 25°, 55°, 80°, 100°, 125°, 150°, 168° measured counterclockwise from +X on x=3cos t, y=2sin t — giving bounces spread from the right shoulder, over the crown, to the left shoulder so the outbound and return legs cross in the middle of the room, matching the source's woven crossing pattern.

DISCRETE CONTROLS (implement every one of these in #ui, each must work independently):
[
  {
