}

NOTES: Render the dome as two nested half-ellipsoid meshes (outer with THREE.BackSide off, inner with side=BackSide so the interior is lit) plus a thin torus-like rim strip along the cut; use a vertical gradient via a ShaderMaterial or a 1D CanvasTexture mapped to Y for both the blue exterior and the tan interior. Cut away the front with a clipping plane (renderer.localClippingEnabled = true, THREE.Plane normal (0,0,-1) at z=1.1) applied to the shell materials only, so the floor and rays stay whole. Rays as Line2/LineSegments2 for constant screen-space width; arrowheads as small flat cone meshes or sprite triangles oriented along each segment. Hit-testing for click: use invisible fat cylinders along each outbound segment as raycast proxies. All-rays view draws all seven at full opacity; single-ray view dims the others to ~12% opacity rather than hiding them so the fan context is retained. Animation: a small emissive sphere per ray advancing along the polyline at constant speed with all pulses sharing one normalized time parameter (path length identical), so they visibly reconverge at F simultaneously; add a soft expanding ring pulse at F' on launch and at F on arrival. Keep labels as HTML/CSS2DRenderer overlays anchored to the focus dots so they stay upright while orbiting. Lighting: hemisphere light plus one soft directional key from upper-left; disable shadows and rely on the gradient textures for the illustrative shading.

